{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the one who offered on the first day</b> etc. <b>Nahshon.</b> The tribe of Judah is first in all things — both in the standards, in the dedication of the altar, in war, in the inheritance of the land, and in the future redemption. In all of them it says קרבנו, but for Nahshon, who was first, it says וקרבנו. And the reason is so that he not grow proud over the others and say, 'I am first among all.' Therefore it began with him וקרבנו, as if he were second to the others, while for all the rest it says קרבנו, as if each and every one were first. And for this reason it did not designate him with the title נשיא, whereas for all the rest who offered after him, it designated each one as נשיא."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:30:37.986830018Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}